/E <50352080204A554E452032303235>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (End-User Data Control)
/E (End-User Data Control)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Gaining Visibility into Employee AI usage is where most enterprises begin their AI security journey. The natural starting point is monitoring and controlling the input of sensitive data into third-party models. Early in the adoption of AI, it was unclear whether models hosted on platforms like Hugging Face would become the standard or if proprietary options like ChatGPT and Claude would dominate. Over time, it has become clear that most employees are gravitating towards a smaller number of options - usually their workforce AI tool, such as Microsoft Co-Pilot or Gemini, or ChatGPT.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
544 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The core security concerns in this category include:)
/E (The core security concerns in this category include:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
545 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 393 0 R
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As specific AI tools have matured, their use cases have also evolved. For example, Cursor is widely used for code generation, while Microsoft Copilot has gained traction for enterprise no-code AI applications.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (For tools like Microsoft Copilot, the main concern is permissions management. Users may unknowingly have access to sensitive data or create applications with broader permissions than intended, which the AI can then leverage to fetch privileged data. This has highlighted a growing need for tighter SaaS identity and access management.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (For secure code generation, typically through Cursor, many organizations have accepted the productivity benefits despite the security tradeoffs of exposing code to third-party models. The focus has shifted towards maintaining code quality and ensuring AI-generated code aligns with organizational standards.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
549 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To summarize, end-user data control revolves around three key subcategories:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
550 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1696 0 R
/E (Data loss prevention via AI chatbots)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
551 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1697 0 R
/E (SaaS access control for AI tooling within productivity platforms)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
552 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1698 0 R
/E (Secure code creation, particularly with developer-facing tools like Cursor)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
