<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Palo Alto Networks recently entered into this unification category through their acquisition of Protect AI, who was focused primarily on model testing. Through this acquisition, Palo Alto provides AI security through both their network security offerings as well as an option for application security adopters. )
/Pg 28 0 R
>>
endobj
683 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The value of having a unified tool will depend on your use case. In general, these tools excel for companies that were first concerned with employee monitoring and sensitive data detection use cases. Their offerings are most mature at detecting and blocking suspicious or unwanted AI activity. They have strong detection engines that extend into developer workflow options via SDK and API usage. )
/Pg 28 0 R
>>
endobj
684 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Broadly speaking, these platforms aim to serve as long-term partners for enterprises managing AI security holistically.)
/Pg 28 0 R
>>
