/Pg 31 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
708 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (From an engineering perspective, application usage of large language models \(LLMs\) is clearly emerging as the primary source of long-term risk. This has unexpectedly led to a resurgence of RASP-like solutions, where developers import an SDK and wrap their AI calls to enable runtime monitoring and protection.)
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
709 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
710 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Lakera also made a strong entrance with their widely-shared Gandalf prompt injection testing game, and have since evolved their platform into one of the most prominent runtime protection solutions for AI application security.)
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
711 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This space is expected to become increasingly competitive as ADR \(Application Detection and Response\) providers expand into runtime AI protection. These platforms already collect much of the data needed for monitoring AI usage at runtime, and in many cases, securing AI usage is not much different from securing any other form of application behavior.)
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
712 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Among them, Operant stands out as one of the most robust runtime protection solutions. It offers both an SDK-based and traditional integration model, enabling features like in-flight sensitive data redaction and full coverage of runtime application behavior.)
/Pg 31 0 R
>>
endobj
