<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The core question underlying any tool-buying decision in AI security is simple: how much risk does AI usage introduce to your company?)
/E (The core question underlying any tool-buying decision in AI security is simple: how much risk does AI usage introduce to your company?)
/Pg 36 0 R
>>
endobj
747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This is a particularly difficult risk to assess because AI-related risk tends to shift rapidly, from negligible to substantial, with just a few small but meaningful architectural changes.)
/Pg 36 0 R
>>
endobj
748 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (If users are primarily interacting with standard chatbots that have secure settings enabled, the risk is relatively low. These sessions are typically limited to the local context provided to the model, which simply responds to input without accessing external systems or data.)
/Pg 36 0 R
>>
endobj
